# dnsmasq for the static i486-musl image: DHCP + DNS for the LAN (see
# monolith-router --dhcp). No dbus IPC surface, no lease-change script exec
# surface, no NLS, IPv4-only (project-wide), no DNSSEC (needs a trust anchor;
# deferred), no TFTP (netboot is deferred behind persistence + an initrd-mod
# selection UI).
#
# dhcp: our global USE="-*" (make.conf) strips dnsmasq's default +dhcp, so
# without this the daemon compiles with -DNO_DHCP — a DNS-only resolver, which
# is useless for SP3. Enable it explicitly to build the DHCP server in.
#
# -static: counter-intuitive, but required and does NOT make the binary dynamic.
# Static linking on this image comes from env/static.conf's LDFLAGS
# (-no-pie -static, applied to */* via package.env) — NOT from this USE flag.
# dnsmasq's ebuild uses the `static` flag only to emit -DHAVE_DNSSEC_STATIC,
# which makes its upstream Makefile link -lgmp unconditionally (even with
# -dnssec). With DNSSEC off there is no static libgmp in the sysroot, so that
# link fails ("cannot find -lgmp"). Turning the USE flag off drops the stray
# gmp dependency while static.conf still delivers a fully static dnsmasq — no
# nettle/gmp pulled into the image.
net-dns/dnsmasq dhcp -static -dbus -script -nls -ipv6 -dnssec -tftp
